8,Nilo,http://www.languagesgulper.com/eng/Nilo.html,"Nilo-Saharan is one of the four major African language phyla, together with Afro-Asiatic, Niger-Congo and Khoisan.",Olu’bo,Nilo-Saharan
9,Nilo-Saharan Languages - SourceWatch,https://www.sourcewatch.org/index.php/Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan Languages are a family of 205 languages. The most common are Dholuo in Kenya and Kanuri in Nigeria with 3.5 million speakers each. The next largest, measured by number of speakers are: Kalenjin; Dinka, Lugbara; Lango; Maa; Acholi; Lendu; Ngambay...",Olu’bo,Nilo-Saharan
